  "design": {
    "entrance": "A slow camera approach through three parallax star layers and drifting nebula; the letters drift in from deep space as points of light, linked by fading constellation lines, and lock into place.",
    "reveal": "On the impact frame the star crests the planet's limb: the atmosphere ignites, a restrained anamorphic flare crosses the frame and the metal letters catch a warm sunrise rim.",
    "camera": "Continuous forward dolly (star layers expand at different rates = parallax), gentle drift.",
    "material": "Dark blue-steel with cool space reflections and a warm sunrise rim from below; glyphs are born as emissive star points that cool into metal.",
    "exit": "The camera keeps travelling: it flies through the title, which swells past the lens as stars stretch."
  },
  "fusion_notes": [
    "Per-glyph constellation convergence is approximated in Fusion by a point-cell dissolve plus scale/blur convergence of the whole title (TextPlus has no per-character transforms without a Follower modifier).",
    "Star layers are pEmitter fields rendered by pRender and scaled by expressions for parallax."
  ],
